---
import Funnel from '../layouts/Funnel.astro';
import BrandHeader from '../components/BrandHeader.astro';
import BrandFooter from '../components/BrandFooter.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import '../styles/funnel-v5.css';
const phases=[
  {name:'The Reading',title:'Recognize the pattern.',body:'Map what happens, what you tell yourself and how you respond. Look at familiar rules about money, responsibility and approval.',output:'A written map of one recurring pattern.'},
  {name:'The Move',title:'Change your next response.',body:'Work through a decision you keep postponing or a request you want to decline. Choose a response that reflects what matters to you and practice it.',output:'One decision. One response to practice.'},
  {name:'The Hold',title:'Build a way to follow through.',body:'Make a plan for using what you learn. Decide how to return after an interruption and review what you need to adjust.',output:'A plan you can return to after a setback.'},
];
---
<Funnel title="Stop starting over | Protocol 44" description="Learn to recognize recurring patterns, question old expectations and follow through. Explore Protocol 44 and try the free quiz and first written exercise.">
  <BrandHeader page="home" />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="product-hero wrap" aria-labelledby="product-title">
      <div class="product-hero-copy"><h1 id="product-title">Stop starting over.<br />Make your <span class="promise-outcome">progress last.</span></h1><p class="hero-intro">Learn to spot the patterns that pull you back, challenge the expectations behind them, and follow through on the changes you want to make.</p><p class="hero-description">Protocol 44 is a guided personal development program that connects self-understanding with practice. Work on decisions about money, making room for yourself, and choosing what you want.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/quiz">Find my starting point <Arrow /></a><p class="button-note">Free quiz. 10 questions. Your result and first exercise, with no email needed.</p><a href="#inside" class="hero-secondary">See what’s inside</a></div>
      <figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/brand/quiet-practice-v5.webp" width="1536" height="1024" alt="A woman writing in a notebook at a kitchen table in afternoon light" fetchpriority="high" /></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="recognition-section wrap" data-motion aria-labelledby="recognition-title"><h2 id="recognition-title">You can see the pattern.<br />Now work on changing it.</h2><div><p class="lead">You make progress, then start second-guessing it. You say yes when you want to say no. You put off a money decision and carry the worry into another week.</p><p>If you’ve tried journaling, affirmations or visualization, you may already know a lot about what you want. Protocol 44 focuses on the next part: noticing your response in an ordinary moment and practicing a different one.</p></div></section>
    <section class="product-inside wrap" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title"><div class="section-heading" data-motion><h2 id="inside-title">A clear path from<br />insight to action.</h2><div><p>The planned program combines 22 lessons and 22 guided audio practices, with worksheets that turn each idea into something to try in your own life.</p><p>The lessons explain what to look for. The audios guide you through reflection and rehearsal. The worksheets help you decide what to do and review what happened.</p></div></div><div class="product-phases">{phases.map((p,i)=><article class="product-phase"><div><span class="phase-order" aria-label={`Phase ${i+1}`}>{i+1}</span><h3>{p.name}</h3></div><div><h4>{p.title}</h4><p>{p.body}</p></div><p class="phase-output">{p.output}</p></article>)}</div><p class="availability-note">The full program is in preparation. Explore the first written sample below; enrollment and recordings are not available yet.</p></section>
    <section class="example-section" aria-labelledby="example-title"><div class="wrap example-layout"><div data-motion><h2 id="example-title">See where the<br />response can change.</h2><p>Maya missed one spending review, then avoided her notebook for a week. The exercise looks at the thought and decision that followed the missed session.</p><p class="example-disclosure">Maya is a fictional example from the first lesson.</p><a href="/vsl#first-practice" class="button button-dark">Try the exercise <Arrow /></a></div><div id="example-story" class="example-workbook"><div class="example-controls" role="group" aria-label="Explore Maya’s example"><button type="button" data-example-step="0" aria-pressed="true">What happened</button><button type="button" data-example-step="1" aria-pressed="false">What she thought</button><button type="button" data-example-step="2" aria-pressed="false">What she could try</button></div><div data-example-panel="0"><h3>She missed her Sunday review.</h3><p>Maya planned ten minutes to review the week’s expenses. A family visit ran late, and she missed her usual time.</p><p class="example-question">Start with what happened.</p></div><div data-example-panel="1" hidden><h3>“I never stick with this.”</h3><p>That is what Maya told herself the next morning. She noticed avoiding the notebook for the rest of the week.</p><p class="example-question">Notice the thought that followed.</p></div><div data-example-panel="2" hidden><h3>Open the notebook.<br />Check one bill.</h3><p>On Monday, Maya can take one small step and schedule the rest of the review separately.</p><p class="example-question">Choose something she could do now.</p></div></div></div></section>
    <section class="fit-section wrap" data-motion><h2>Bring it into the<br />decisions that matter.</h2><div><p class="lead">The aim is to give you a way to act on what you understand about yourself. Choose an everyday situation you want to handle differently.</p><ul class="plain-list"><li>Face a money decision you’ve been putting off.</li><li>Set a boundary instead of agreeing automatically.</li><li>Question a “should” you no longer want to live by.</li><li>Return to a plan after a difficult day.</li></ul></div></section>
    <section class="faq-section wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><h2 id="faq-title">A few questions<br />you might have</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What will I get from the quiz?</summary><p>You’ll choose a focus, see a reflection based on your answers, and get a practical question and exercise to begin with. The result is free and appears immediately. No email is required.</p></details><details><summary>What if I’ve tried something like this before?</summary><p>Start by seeing what you’ll actually do. The sample asks you to describe a setback, notice the thought that followed, and choose a specific response. You can try it before deciding whether the approach fits you.</p></details><details><summary>What if the result doesn’t feel right?</summary><p>You can change your focus or review your answers. The quiz suggests a topic to explore; it doesn’t tell you who you are.</p></details><details><summary>How will the audio exercises work?</summary><p>Each planned audio is paired with a lesson. It will guide reflection and rehearsal, with pauses to consider how the idea applies to your situation. You then choose an action and review it in writing. The recordings are in preparation.</p></details><details><summary>Is the full program available?</summary><p>It is still in preparation. The first written sample is available now. The final schedule, access terms and support details will be shared before enrollment opens.</p></details><details><summary>Is this therapy?</summary><p>Protocol 44 is educational self-reflection. It does not provide a clinical assessment or replace professional care. Choose manageable situations for the sample and pause whenever you need.</p></details></div></section>
    <section class="product-close wrap" data-motion><img src="/brand/symbol-ink.svg" alt="" width="90" height="90" /><h2>Start with the pattern<br />you’re ready to change.</h2><p>Choose your starting point and turn one familiar setback into a decision you can act on.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/quiz">Find my starting point <Arrow /></a></section>
  </main><BrandFooter />
  <script>import '../lib/page-motion';</script>
</Funnel>
